IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand), 2019 No 58 -- LAYER 1: NOUNS.
-- Nouns only: no rule and no directive. A witness of ordinary competence could testify to each fact below
-- without reading the Act; what the facts amount to is decided in the modules that import this one.

§ `Instruments`

-- What a person can say about how an instrument was made (the facts s 5(1) "secondary legislation" asks).
DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `it is made under an Act, directly or indirectly`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act, or other legislation, states that it is secondary legislation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is made under the Royal prerogative`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `its form and purpose are set out in Schedule 1A`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- `the whole of an Act` and `a part of an Act` are the two things s 5(1) "legislation means the whole or a part of an Act" names; `an Act` is the printed phrase for either.
DECLARE `Kind of enactment or instrument` IS ONE OF
    `an Act`
    `the whole of an Act`
    `a part of an Act`
    `secondary legislation`
    `an instrument that is not legislation`
    `a Bill not yet enacted`

§ `People and bodies`

-- The kinds of person the Act's rules of reading speak of (ss 13, 16).
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a body corporate`
    `an unincorporated body`

§ `Numbers of words`

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF
    singular
    plural
